  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "PR metadata must be representable as GitHub CLI arguments before artifact application; rejected text is preserved privately and cannot trigger repeated publication.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution_result.mjs",
        "lib/public_output.mjs",
        "lib/block.mjs",
        "lib/gh.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/commands/resume.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "The existing typed publication validator checks title and raw body for NUL before normalization, head/tracked-path/mode reads, applying artifacts, verification, push or PR publication.",
        "Raw-body validation also rejects NUL in a replaceable recovery block, preventing normalization from silently repairing an invalid provider payload.",
        "Artifact, pushed-head and legacy verified paths persist reason result-validation and phase blocked before writes. Verified checkpoints retain fingerprint, applied head, paths and original evidence bytes.",
        "The existing coordinator settles the actual provider exit and nullable cost once, preserves private result bytes across restart, refuses recheck and permits one explicit continuation in the same session.",
        "Unrelated review reaches done while the rejected root remains blocked. Collection and unavailable Git metadata retain their existing retryable behavior.",
        "Shared NUL validation protects create/edit result publication, direct title/body/comment writes, labels and recovery-only migration. Ordinary writes invoke no subprocess for rejected input; recovery migration performs only its necessary fresh read.",
        "Recovery-only migration still preserves legacy prose and opaque identity without enforcing the separate branding rule; both raw and normalized bodies are checked for NUL.",
        "Errors and public violation lists identify the field without echoing rejected text. Quotes, literal backslash-zero sequences, Unicode, CRLF and multiline text remain byte-for-byte unchanged.",
        "Native execFile argument validation produces ERR_INVALID_ARG_VALUE for a NUL argument before spawning. The production boundary now classifies the same input as deterministic publication rejection instead of retrying that subprocess error.",
        "No model/provider defaults, credentials, execution permissions, paid-call scope, transport availability or human merge boundaries were changed."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "NUL PR metadata blocks before artifact application and preserves verified recovery evidence",
        "deterministic publication rejection settles once and permits an explicit corrective continuation (nulTitle, nulBody and nulRecoveryBody)",
        "GitHub writers reject NUL metadata before writes, including recovery-only migration",
        "public text rejects NUL bytes without exposing or rewriting metadata",
        "GitHub metadata migration reads the current body and preserves prose, and mismatched identity writes nothing",
        "collection and unavailable publication I/O remain pending and recover without another dispatch",
        "a rejected result cannot settle until its blocked checkpoint is durable"
      ]
    }
  ],
